  "full_text": "23 captures\n\n17 Nov 2021 - 23 Feb 2026\n\nJan\n\nFEB\n\nMar\n\n23\n\n2025\n\n2026\n\n2027\n\nsuccess\n\nfail\n\nAbout this capture\n\nCOLLECTED BY\n\nCollection: Save Page Now\n\nTIMESTAMPS\n\nThe Wayback Machine - https://web.archive.org/web/20260223193939/https://www.hairstonforpeace.com/\n\n0\n\nSkip to Content\n\nHome\n\nAbout\n\nPlatform\n\nSupporters\n\nPosters\n\nVolunteer\n\nDonate\n\nOpen Menu Close Menu\n\nHome\n\nAbout\n\nPlatform\n\nSupporters\n\nPosters\n\nVolunteer\n\nDonate\n\nOpen Menu Close Menu\n\nHome\n\nAbout\n\nPlatform\n\nSupporters\n\nPosters\n\nVolunteer\n\nDonate\n\nAndrew Hairston is a civil rights attorney and writer running for Justice of the Peace in Travis County Precinct 1. A proud Black southerner, man of faith, and democratic socialist, Andrew is committed to building a justice system rooted in care, not punishment.\n\nAndrew believes our courts should serve the people with compassion, dignity, and integrity. He’s running to ensure that justice in Travis County means housing stability, community safety, and a legal system that works for everyone.\n\nMake a Donation to the Campaign\n\nSign up with your email address to receive news and updates.\n\nEmail Address\n\nSign Up\n\nThank you!\n\nDonate Contact Follow\n\nPol. Ad. paid for by Andrew Hairston for Justice of the Peace, Pct. 1; Gabriella Zeidan, Treasurer. In compliance with all applicable laws & regulations. P.O. Box 300615 Austin, TX 78703",
